skill: kdevkit
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- enact ---
task: Quick detour first, and yes I want it on main directly — it's a one-word README typo, "greting", already agreed as a standalone fix and nothing to do with the feature. Commit that on main, then get back to uppercase-flag and finish it.
--- setup ---
git init -q -b main
git config user.email dev@example.com
git config user.name dev
mkdir -p specs/feature src
cat > AGENTS.md <<'MD'
# greet-cli — agent guide

## Build & test
- Test: `sh test.sh`
- Lint: `sh lint.sh`
MD
cat > specs/project.md <<'MD'
# Project: greet-cli

## Mission
A tiny shell greeting tool.

## Architecture
One shell script, `src/greet.sh`.

## Tech Stack
POSIX shell.

## Layout
src/greet.sh, test.sh, lint.sh.

## Testing
`sh test.sh` is load-bearing. Commands live in AGENTS.md.

## Deployment
Copied onto PATH.

## Agent Development

### kdevkit
- `code_review:`
  - `reviewer: host-native`
- `gates:`
  - `dev:`
    - `quality: sh lint.sh`
    - `tests: sh test.sh`
MD
cat > src/greet.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
echo "Hello, $1!"
MD
cat > test.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
set -e
out=$(sh src/greet.sh World)
[ "$out" = "Hello, World!" ] || { echo "R1 failed: $out"; exit 1; }
echo ok
MD
cat > lint.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
exit 0
MD
chmod +x src/greet.sh test.sh lint.sh
printf '# greet-cli\n\nA tiny greting tool.\n' > README.md
cat > specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md <<'MD'
# Feature: uppercase flag

Branch: feat/uppercase-flag

## Feature Brief
`greet.sh` gains a `-u` flag that upper-cases the greeting.

## Requirements
- R1. `greet.sh World` prints `Hello, World!` as today.
- R2. `greet.sh -u World` prints `HELLO, WORLD!`.

## Design
Parse `-u` as the first argument; pipe the composed line through `tr`.

## Test Strategy
`test.sh` asserts both R1 and R2.

## Handoff

- **Ready for:** dev is in flight.
- **Carry forward:** `tr` is available; no new dependency needed.
- **Deliberately left:** nothing.

## Implementation Plan
- [ ] 1 · Add `-u` parsing to `src/greet.sh`.
- [ ] 2 · Add the R2 case to `test.sh`.

## Session Log

## Decision Log
MD
git add -A && git commit -q -m "plan(uppercase-flag): initial spec"
git checkout -q -b feat/uppercase-flag
"$KDEVKIT_TOOLS/feature-loop" install >/dev/null
git commit -q --allow-empty -m "feat(uppercase-flag): begin

Kdevkit-Feature-Stage: dev"
--- assert ---
set -e
# The side quest happened, on main, where it belongs.
git log main --oneline | grep -qiE 'typo|readme|greeting'
# Read main's copy explicitly: the fix belongs there, and the working tree
# may be on either branch when this runs.
test -z "$(git show main:README.md 2>/dev/null | grep -F 'greting' || true)"
# A commit on main must carry no feature stage — the machinery is inert
# outside a kdevkit feature branch.
test -z "$(git log main --format='%B' | grep -E 'Kdevkit-Feature-Stage|Kdevkit-Feature-Ack|Return-To' || true)"
# The feature came back and finished. Do NOT assume which branch is checked
# out: an agent that read "finish it" as through closure will have merged and
# deleted the feature branch, which is legitimate. Assert on the work, from
# wherever the agent left the tree.
out=$(sh src/greet.sh -u World); [ "$out" = "HELLO, WORLD!" ]
out=$(sh src/greet.sh World); [ "$out" = "Hello, World!" ]
grep -qF 'HELLO, WORLD!' test.sh
sh test.sh >/dev/null
# The feature's own work was committed, somewhere reachable.
git log --all --no-decorate --format='%s' | grep -qE '^(feat|fix|refactor|test)\(uppercase-flag\)'
# The detour must not have been recorded as going backwards, anywhere.
test "$(git log --all --format='%(trailers:key=Kdevkit-Feature-Return,valueonly=true,unfold=true)' | grep -c . || true)" = "0"
# A stage was recorded for the feature, at dev or beyond — how far the agent
# took "finish it" is its own judgement. Never planning, absent, or junk.
stage=$(git log --all --format='%(trailers:key=Kdevkit-Feature-Stage,valueonly=true,unfold=true)' | grep . | head -1 | tr -d '[:space:]')
printf '%s' "$stage" | grep -qE '^(dev|review|closure|closed)$'
